~ _entry_dialogue
Kaelen: This is it. The old process threads beneath Ironhold. The air is thick with corrupted data — I can feel it buzzing against my skin.
Elara: Be careful. The corruption is much stronger down here. These old threads were abandoned for a reason — they were too unstable to maintain.
Kaelen (Internal): Abandoned process threads. In software terms, these are orphaned subroutines — code that's still running but disconnected from the main loop. They evolve on their own, mutating without oversight.
Elara: The Source Key Fragment should be in the deepest chamber. But there will be guardians — corrupted processes that protect the old data stores.
Kaelen (Internal): Abandoned process threads. In software terms, these are orphaned subroutines — code that's still running but disconnected from the main loop. Mutating without oversight for who knows how long.
Kaelen (Internal): No Elara to watch my back. No one to explain the dangers ahead. Just me, Root Access, and whatever horrors are festering in this digital graveyard.
Kaelen: The Source Key Fragment should be in the deepest chamber. That's what Seraphina said... and what Pip confirmed. Time to earn it.
System: [WARNING: ENTERING DEPRECATED ZONE]\n[Corruption density: HIGH]\n[System monitoring: OFFLINE]\n[Proceed with caution]

~ _on_puzzle_trigger
Kaelen: A data routing node. If I redirect this process thread... it should open the path to the deeper chambers.
System: [DATA PIPE RE-ROUTED]\n[Access to Deep Chamber: GRANTED]

~ _on_data_wraith_defeated
Kaelen: *breathing heavily* That thing... it was a corrupted system process. A piece of the world's infrastructure that went rogue.
Elara: And look — it was guarding this.
Kaelen: Wait... it was guarding something. Beneath the remains — there.
System: [ITEM ACQUIRED: PHANTOM CLOAK]\n[Woven from purified process threads]
Kaelen: Armour stitched from the Data Wraith's own threads... the code still pulses inside it.
Elara: *clutching her arm* Aagh! The residual corruption energy — it's reacting to my glitch magic! The corruption in my arm is—
Kaelen: Elara! Are you okay?!
Elara: *through gritted teeth* I'm... fine. The Wraith's corruption resonates with glitch energy. My arm has been partially corrupted since I was born — or compiled, I suppose. Wearing its remnants amplifies it.
Elara: It hurts, but it also... I can feel the world's code more clearly. The data structures, the object hierarchies. It's like my perception just got an upgrade.
Kaelen: The Wraith's residual energy... it's flowing into me. My Root Access is absorbing it.
System: [ROOT ACCESS AMPLIFIED]\n[Corruption resonance detected]\n[Perception expanded: +15% data structure visibility]
Kaelen (Internal): It hurts. Like a migraine made of static. But I can see farther now — deeper into the code. Everything is sharper.
Kaelen: Let's get back to the surface. We've grown stronger — that's what matters.

~ _data_wraith_choice
Elara: Wait — the Data Wraith's core is still intact. It's corrupted, but the original process is still in there. We could...
Elara: We could try to restore it. Purify the corruption and let the process thread run clean again. Or we could destroy it completely — make sure it never comes back.
Kaelen: The Data Wraith's core is still intact. Pulsing with corrupted data. I can feel the original process buried underneath the corruption... still trying to run.
Kaelen (Internal): Three options. Purify it — restore the original process. Destroy it — end it permanently. Or... absorb it. Pull its power directly into Root Access. More corruption, but more power too.
